# Sprint 23 — Privileged Group Membership Detection Engineering

**Status:** Complete 
**Detection:** DET-005 — Privileged Domain Group Membership Change 
**MITRE ATT&CK:** T1098.007 — Account Manipulation: Additional Local or Domain Groups 
**Primary Data Source:** Windows Security Event Logs 
**Primary Event:** Event ID 4728 — Member Added to a Security-Enabled Global Group 
**SIEM:** Splunk Enterprise

---

# Objective

Develop, validate, and operationalize a detection for additions to privileged Active Directory security groups.

Sprint 23 expanded the SOC lab into identity-based privilege escalation and account manipulation monitoring.

The primary controlled behavior was:

```text
Standard Domain Account
        |
        v
Added to Domain Admins
        |
        v
Windows Security Event 4728
        |
        v
Splunk Enterprise
        |
        v
DET-005
        |
        v
High-Severity Alert
```

The sprint focused on:

- Validating DC01 security telemetry
- Creating a dedicated test account
- Establishing a privileged-group membership baseline
- Generating controlled Domain Admin membership changes
- Analyzing Windows Event ID 4728
- Developing DET-005
- Performing positive and negative validation
- Creating a privileged-group hunting query
- Operationalizing DET-005 as a Splunk alert
- Mapping activity to MITRE ATT&CK T1098.007
- Developing an analyst investigation workflow
- Correlating identity activity with existing detections
- Cleaning up all temporary privileged access

